{
  "name": "robot-ring-fight",
  "description": "Two cells for the scheduling battle (R5): gnb0 serves ue0 and gnb1 serves ue1, each pair through its own broker process. gnb1 stands on gnb0's mast: the two brokers carry no inter-cell link, so co-location costs nothing and makes the two links statistically identical -- only the GPU/CPU scheduling of the two brokers differs. For the same reason both robots stand still on the line-of-sight side of the ring, mirrored about the mast axis (R1 coverage: -1.6..-2.9 dB there), so neither link carries a pillar shadow the other does not. The arena's live position feed overrides these positions in the demo.",
